--- .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap27/review_prompt1.txt
Review the uncommitted stmap27 AutoEDA iteration in this ABC repository.

Project constraints:
- The project pack in .autoeda/project_pack/agent.md is binding.
- stmap27 must preserve map and all prior stmap0..stmap26 behavior.
- The new command must be registered, buildable, and provide -h usage.
- The evaluation flow is read_lib 7nm_lvt_ff.lib; read <design>; resyn; resyn2; dch -v; stmap27; topo; buffer; upsize -v; dnsize -v; stime.
- Required benchmarks are benchmarks/i10.aig, benchmarks/ode.abc.blif, benchmarks/or1200.abc.blif, and benchmarks/syn2.abc.blif.

What changed:
- Added src/base/abci/abcStmap_27.c and registered stmap27.
- Added mapper mode fSkipFanout=28.
- stmap27 keeps stmap24/stmap21 strong deep behavior and reopens the moderate deep slack band only when a candidate avoids the high-reference, low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26.
- It records signature seed/block diagnostics and stats.

Validation already run before this review:
- make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1
- ./abc -c "stmap27 -h"
- smoke on benchmarks/i10.aig with the full downstream stime flow
- baseline and candidate flows on all four required benchmarks
- parsed final stime metrics and signature diagnostics
- CEC on all four required benchmarks using original and post-flow strashed AIGs
- artifact completeness check

Please review for correctness risks, missed version integration, broken older stmap behavior, command/help issues, mapper-mode gating errors, diagnostic/logging inconsistencies, evaluation artifact problems, and any required follow-up before this iteration can be counted. Lead with findings and cite concrete files/lines where possible.
