The new stmap27 mode does not update the risk counters needed by the existing adaptive profile gate, causing incorrect mapping behavior for that mode on large designs.

Review comment:

- [P2] Include stmap27 in profile counters — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:748-748
  When `p->fSkipFanout == 28`, this path now treats stmap27 as an stmap13+ mode, but the immediately called `Map_MatchStmap13CountRisk()` still returns early for modes greater than 27. On large stmap27 runs the lower/upper/exact-risk counters therefore stay at zero, so `Map_MatchHasStmap15ReliefProfile()` never opens the adaptive profile and the new mode keeps applying the pre-profile fallback after it should have relaxed.
